<aside class="public-email-tutorial" aria-labelledby="public-email-tutorial-title">
  <div class="public-email-tutorial-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="public-email-tutorial-eyebrow">FIRST Dashboard setup</p>
      <h2 id="public-email-tutorial-title">Add a public team email</h2>
      <p>An adult team contact with profile access can add the address. Use an inbox the team checks regularly because verification codes will be sent there.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://my.firstinspires.org/Dashboard/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open FIRST Dashboard <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>

  <ol class="public-email-tutorial-steps">
    <li>
      <span class="public-email-tutorial-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <img src="/assets/img/public-email-tutorial/step-1-team-profile.webp" alt="Illustration of My Teams with the Team Profile settings control highlighted" width="900" height="675" loading="lazy">
      <h3>Open the team profile</h3>
      <p>Sign in, find the team under <strong>My Teams</strong>, and open its profile or team information settings.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="public-email-tutorial-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <img src="/assets/img/public-email-tutorial/step-2-public-email.webp" alt="Illustration of a Team Profile form with the Public Email field highlighted" width="900" height="675" loading="lazy">
      <h3>Enter the public email</h3>
      <p>Choose the edit option and add a monitored team address in the <strong>Public Email</strong> field.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="public-email-tutorial-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <img src="/assets/img/public-email-tutorial/step-3-save-profile.webp" alt="Illustration of saving a public email and receiving a profile-updated confirmation" width="900" height="675" loading="lazy">
      <h3>Save, then try again</h3>
      <p>Save the profile, allow a few minutes for the public listing to update, then request a new verification code here.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="public-email-tutorial-note"><strong>Can’t edit the profile?</strong> Ask the team’s Lead Coach/Mentor or another authorized adult contact to make the change.</p>
</aside>
